==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-crash course.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} A [[quick]], [[intense]] course of [[learning]], especially one which is [[informal]] or [[hurried]].
#: {{uxi|en|He got a '''crash course''' in babysitting when his sister dropped off his nephew for the afternoon.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2015|author=James Lambert|editors=Lan Li; Jamie McKeown; Liming Liu|chapter=Lexicography as a teaching tool: A Hong Kong case study|title=Dictionaries and corpora: Innovations in reference science. Proceedings of ASIALEX 2015 Hong Kong|publisher=The Hong Kong Polytechnic University|location=Hong Kong|page=145|passage=Students were essentially given a ‘'''crash course'''’ in how to be a lexicographer over a number of tutorial classes, beginning with lexicographical data collection.}}

